data: {"type":"data-guide","id":"guide","data":{"slug":"gmail","permalink":"/guides/gmail","guide":{"verdict":{"tier":"review_required","summary":"Register the OAuth client, configure the required Gmail scopes and Composio callback, and complete Google's review before public use. Gmail is categorized as a restricted scope, and sensitive scopes require review by Google.","effort_hours":{"min":1.0,"max":3.0},"calendar":{"min_days":0.0,"max_days":null,"label":"Planning estimate: no official review wait is stated"},"calendar_basis":"estimate","confidence":"medium"},"situations":{"questions":[{"id":"users","text":"Who will connect Gmail accounts?","options":[{"id":"own_org","label":"Only my organization"},{"id":"outside","label":"Outside users"}]},{"id":"actions","text":"What must the agent do with Gmail?","options":[{"id":"read","label":"Read messages or metadata"},{"id":"write_send","label":"Write data or send messages"}]}],"variants":[{"when":{"users":"own_org","actions":"read"},"tier":"review_required","summary":"An internal Gmail OAuth app still needs the appropriate Gmail scopes and Google review where sensitive or restricted scopes are used.","calendar_label":"Review wait is unknown","notes":["Gmail is categorized as a restricted scope.","Choose the narrowest suitable scope; Google advises avoiding sensitive scopes when possible."]},{"when":{"users":"own_org","actions":"write_send"},"tier":"review_required","summary":"An internal app that writes or sends must request the corresponding authorization scopes and complete Google's applicable scope review.","calendar_label":"Review wait is unknown","notes":["Sensitive OAuth scopes require review by Google."]},{"when":{"users":"outside","actions":"read"},"tier":"review_required","summary":"A public app exposing Gmail user data must use the External user type, select its scopes, and complete Google's verification process.","calendar_label":"Review wait is unknown","notes":["For use outside the Google Workspace organization, the app must use the External user type.","Public applications using scopes that permit access to certain user data must complete verification."]},{"when":{"users":"outside","actions":"write_send"},"tier":"review_required","summary":"A public app that writes or sends requires External user type, least-privilege scopes, and Google's verification and sensitive-scope review.","calendar_label":"Review wait is unknown","notes":["The app must define its required authorization scopes.","Sensitive scopes require review by Google."]}]},"byo_advice":"Create an OAuth client in Google Cloud, configure its OAuth consent screen and scopes, set the authorized redirect URI to the callback shown in Composio's Gmail auth config, then paste the client ID, client secret, scopes, and any required secret version into Composio. Check the current Google console labels and the exact Composio callback value in those interfaces; Composio's managed Gmail app is enough for standard connections, while a bring-your-own app is appropriate when you need custom scopes, branding, or your own client controls.","before_you_start":[{"text":"The developer console needs a signed-in account: Sign-in page at accounts.google.com.","evidence":{"label":"TESTED","source_id":"s6","quote":null,"found_in":null,"note":"Our read-only probe on 2026-10-22 loaded https://console.cloud.google.com/auth/overview and ended at https://accounts.google.com/v3/signin/identifier?continue=https://console.cloud.google.com/auth/overview&followup=https://console.cloud.google.com/auth/overview&osid=1&passive=1209600&service=cloudconsole&flowName=GlifWebSignIn&flowEntry=ServiceLogin&dsh=S-1978760587:1792649794270925 (login wall)."}},{"text":"Use a Google account with Gmail enabled and have a Google Cloud project available.","evidence":{"label":"UNCERTAIN","source_id":"s2","quote":null,"found_in":null,"note":"Downgraded from DOCS: quote not found on the source page. Original quote: \"A Google account with Gmail enabled.\nA Google Cloud project.\"."}},{"text":"Decide whether each target platform needs its own OAuth client ID.","evidence":{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s2","quote":"If your app runs on multiple platforms, you must create a separate client ID for each platform.","found_in":"visible","note":null}},{"text":"Prefer a non-sensitive scope where possible because many Gmail-related scopes overlap.","evidence":{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s1","quote":"Many scopes overlap, so it's best to use a scope that isn't sensitive.","found_in":"visible","note":null}}],"limits":[{"what":"Gmail connector processing throughput","value":1.0,"unit":"transaction per second per node","scope":"Gmail connector","evidence":{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s3","quote":"The Gmail connector can process a maximum of 1 transaction per second,\nper node, and throttles any transactions beyond this limit.","found_in":"visible","note":null}},{"what":"Default minimum node count","value":2.0,"unit":"nodes","scope":"Default Gmail connection sizing","evidence":{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s3","quote":"If you don't enter any values, by default\nthe minimum nodes are set to 2 (for better availability) and the maximum nodes are set to 50.","found_in":"visible","note":null}},{"what":"Default maximum node count","value":50.0,"unit":"nodes","scope":"Default Gmail connection sizing","evidence":{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s3","quote":"If you don't enter any values, by default\nthe minimum nodes are set to 2 (for better availability) and the maximum nodes are set to 50.","found_in":"visible","note":null}},{"what":"OAuth client IDs required across platforms","value":1.0,"unit":"client ID per platform","scope":"Apps running on multiple platforms","evidence":{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s2","quote":"If your app runs on multiple platforms, you must create a separate client ID for each platform.","found_in":"visible","note":null}}],"steps":[{"n":1,"title":"Prepare access and project","detail":"Sign in to the Google Cloud console, select a Google Cloud project, and ensure billing is enabled if the project is used for the related Google Cloud configuration.","actor":"human","human_reason":"credential","irreversible":false,"values":[],"evidence":{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s4","quote":"Also, make sure that billing is enabled for your Google Cloud project.","found_in":"visible","note":null}},{"n":2,"title":"Register your own OAuth application","detail":"Create an OAuth client for your own Gmail integration. Set the user type to External if the app will be used outside its Google Workspace organization.","actor":"human","human_reason":"credential","irreversible":true,"values":[{"label":"User type","value":"External"},{"label":"OAuth client type","value":"Web server"}],"evidence":{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s2","quote":"In the future, when you create an app for use outside of your Google Workspace organization, you must change the User type to External.","found_in":"visible","note":"The Web server client type follows the documented server-side redirect URI requirement."}},{"n":3,"title":"Configure authorization details","detail":"Enter the Gmail scopes appropriate for your use case and register Composio's callback as the authorized redirect URI. Use only the scopes needed for the agent's intended Gmail operations.","actor":"agent","human_reason":null,"irreversible":true,"values":[{"label":"Authorized redirect URI","value":"https://backend.composio.dev/api/v3/toolkits/auth/callback"},{"label":"Scopes","value":"Gmail API scopes appropriate for the intended Gmail operations"}],"evidence":{"label":"UNCERTAIN","source_id":null,"quote":null,"found_in":null,"note":"The provided claims confirm that server-side apps use authorized redirect URIs and that developers select appropriate Gmail scopes, but they do not directly document the Composio callback value or a complete minimum scope list."}},{"n":4,"title":"Collect credentials","detail":"After Google issues the client ID and client secret, store both securely so they can be entered into the Composio Gmail auth configuration.","actor":"human","human_reason":"credential","irreversible":false,"values":[{"label":"Client ID","value":"Google OAuth client ID"},{"label":"Client secret","value":"Google OAuth client secret"}],"evidence":{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s3","quote":"OAuth 2.0 - Authorization code\nClient ID: Enter the client ID to use for OAuth authentication.\nScopes: Enter a list of desired scopes.\nClient Secret: The client secret to use for OAuth authentication.","found_in":"visible","note":null}},{"n":5,"title":"Create the Composio auth configuration","detail":"Paste the Google client ID, selected scopes, and client secret into Composio's Gmail authorization-code auth configuration, then test the connection flow.","actor":"agent","human_reason":null,"irreversible":false,"values":[{"label":"Authentication","value":"OAuth 2.0 - Authorization code"}],"evidence":{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s3","quote":"The following authentication types are supported by the Gmail connection:\nService Account Authentication\nOAuth 2.0 - JWT Bearer\nOAuth 2.0 - Authorization code","found_in":"visible","note":null}},{"n":6,"title":"Complete review and verification","detail":"Review the OAuth consent screen and submit the app for Google verification when required. Publish the app to production if it is ready to leave testing.","actor":"human","human_reason":"submit","irreversible":true,"values":[],"evidence":{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s4","quote":"Review your OAuth consent screen information, and then click Back to dashboard.","found_in":"visible","note":null}},{"n":7,"title":"Wait for approval before production use","detail":"Do not treat testing access as production approval. Monitor Google's review process and confirm that the app and requested scopes are approved before relying on the connection.","actor":"human","human_reason":"wait","irreversible":false,"values":[],"evidence":{"label":"UNCERTAIN","source_id":null,"quote":null,"found_in":null,"note":"The claims establish that verification or scope review can be required, but do not state the review duration or approval criteria."}}],"review":{"required":"yes","trigger":"Required for sensitive or restricted Gmail scopes and for public applications that access certain user data.","submit":["Configure and review the OAuth consent screen information.","Add test users when testing the OAuth app.","Publish the OAuth app to production if production use is intended.","If an unverified-app message appears during testing, submit a verification request to remove it."],"reviewer":"Google","wait_official":null,"wait_community":null,"cost":null,"evidence":[{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s4","quote":"Review your OAuth consent screen information, and then click Back to dashboard.","found_in":"visible","note":null},{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s4","quote":"If you want to publish your app to production now, click Publish app, and then click Confirm in the confirmation dialog.","found_in":"visible","note":null},{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s1","quote":"If you see unverified\napp on the screen when testing your application, you must submit a\nverification request to remove it.","found_in":"visible","note":null},{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s1","quote":"Sensitive scopes require review by Google","found_in":"visible","note":null},{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s1","quote":"If your public application uses scopes that permit access to\ncertain user data, it must complete a verification process.","found_in":"visible","note":null},{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s5","quote":"Gmail API\nGoogle Drive API\nGoogle Fit API\nGoogle Chat API\nData Portability API\nPhotos Ambient API\nGoogle Health API","found_in":"visible","note":null}]},"customer_gates":[{"text":"An app used outside its Google Workspace organization must use the External user type and define its required authorization scopes.","evidence":{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s2","quote":"In the future, when you create an app for use outside of your Google Workspace organization, you must change the User type to External.","found_in":"visible","note":null}},{"text":"Public applications that request scopes permitting access to certain user data must complete Google's verification process.","evidence":{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s1","quote":"If your public application uses scopes that permit access to\ncertain user data, it must complete a verification process.","found_in":"visible","note":null}},{"text":"Sensitive OAuth scopes require review by Google.","evidence":{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s1","quote":"Sensitive scopes require review by Google","found_in":"visible","note":null}}],"gotchas":[{"text":"For a server-side app, add the callback endpoint under Authorized redirect URIs.","evidence":{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s2","quote":"Server-side apps (Java, Python, and more)–Under Authorized redirect URIs, click Add URI.","found_in":"visible","note":null}},{"text":"If the app runs on multiple platforms, create a separate OAuth client ID for each platform.","evidence":{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s2","quote":"If your app runs on multiple platforms, you must create a separate client ID for each platform.","found_in":"visible","note":null}},{"text":"An existing Google session may skip the account chooser and consent dialog; request a new access token with a consent prompt when no token exists.","evidence":{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s2","quote":"Skip display of account chooser and consent dialog for an existing session.","found_in":"visible","note":"The claim also describes requesting a new access token with a consent prompt when no token exists."}},{"text":"The Gmail API is categorized as a restricted scope, so plan for the corresponding review and policy requirements.","evidence":{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s5","quote":"Gmail API\nGoogle Drive API\nGoogle Fit API\nGoogle Chat API\nData Portability API\nPhotos Ambient API\nGoogle Health API","found_in":"visible","note":null}}],"blockers":[{"symptom":"The testing consent screen shows an unverified-app message.","cause":"The app has not completed Google's required verification request.","fix":"Submit the verification request and remove the message only after the request process is completed.","evidence":{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s1","quote":"If you see unverified\napp on the screen when testing your application, you must submit a\nverification request to remove it.","found_in":"visible","note":null}},{"symptom":"The callback does not return successfully to Composio.","cause":"The OAuth client's authorized redirect URI may be missing or may not exactly match the URI configured in Composio.","fix":"Add the exact Composio callback URI to the Google OAuth client's Authorized redirect URIs and verify the Composio auth configuration.","evidence":{"label":"UNCERTAIN","source_id":null,"quote":null,"found_in":null,"note":"The claims confirm that server-side apps list callback endpoints as authorized redirect URIs, but do not directly document Composio callback behavior."}},{"symptom":"The app cannot move from testing to production.","cause":"Required OAuth scope review or public-app verification has not been completed.","fix":"Review the consent screen, submit any required verification, and publish the app to production after approval.","evidence":{"label":"DOCS","source_id":"s4","quote":"If you want to publish your app to production now, click Publish app, and then click Confirm in the confirmation dialog.","found_in":"visible","note":null}}],"prepared":{"scopes":[{"scope":"Gmail API scope appropriate to the intended Gmail operations","why":"The app needs only the Gmail API access required by the agent; the provided claims do not identify a more specific minimum scope.","review_class":"restricted"}],"privacy_policy_outline":["Describe the app developer and its purpose.","Explain the Gmail data accessed and why each requested scope is needed.","Describe how Gmail data is stored, protected, and deleted.","Identify user controls for disconnecting and revoking access."],"consent_screen":{"app_name":"Developer-defined Gmail integration app name","user_support_email":"Developer support email","privacy_policy_url":"Developer-hosted privacy policy URL","purpose":"Explain that the app connects the user's Gmail account so their AI agent can perform the configured Gmail operations.","scopes":"List only the Gmail API scopes required by the intended operations.","logo_and_branding":"Use the developer app's branding and a clear description of its Gmail purpose."},"review_text":"Explain the agent workflow, the exact Gmail operations performed, why each requested scope is necessary, how users grant and revoke access, and the data handling and retention practices. Note that Gmail API access is categorized as a restricted scope and sensitive scopes require Google review."},"open_questions":["What exact minimum Gmail OAuth scope string or strings are required for the intended operations?","Does Google require additional branding, privacy policy, demo video, or verification details for this app?","What is the current review and production-approval duration?","Are there organization-specific administrator restrictions that block your selected scopes or third-party apps?","Which access and refresh token lifetimes apply to the chosen OAuth client configuration?"],"schema_version":"1","slug":"gmail","app_name":"Gmail","guide_type":"generated","last_verified":"2026-10-22","composio":{"toolkit_slug":"gmail","status":"managed","callback_url":"https://backend.composio.dev/api/v3/toolkits/auth/callback","callback_note":"Copy the exact redirect URI shown in your Composio auth config; some toolkits still show the legacy https://backend.composio.dev/api/v1/auth-apps/add."},"wall_probe":{"console_url":"https://console.cloud.google.com/auth/overview","final_url":"https://accounts.google.com/v3/signin/identifier?continue=https://console.cloud.google.com/auth/overview&followup=https://console.cloud.google.com/auth/overview&osid=1&passive=1209600&service=cloudconsole&flowName=GlifWebSignIn&flowEntry=ServiceLogin&dsh=S-1978760587:1792649794270925","redirect_chain":["https://console.cloud.google.com/auth/overview","https://accounts.google.com/ServiceLogin?service=cloudconsole&passive=1209600&osid=1&continue=https://console.cloud.google.com/auth/overview&followup=https://console.cloud.google.com/auth/overview","https://accounts.google.com/v3/signin/identifier?continue=https://console.cloud.google.com/auth/overview&followup=https://console.cloud.google.com/auth/overview&osid=1&passive=1209600&service=cloudconsole&flowName=GlifWebSignIn&flowEntry=ServiceLogin&dsh=S-1978760587:1792649794270925"],"outcome":"login_wall","wall_host":"accounts.google.com","asks_for":"Sign-in page at accounts.google.com","bot_check":false,"method":"http","observed_at":"2026-10-22"},"conflicts":[],"sources":[{"id":"s1","url":"https://developers.google.com/identity/protocols/oauth2/scopes","title":"OAuth 2.0 Scopes for Google APIs | Google for Developers","accessed":"2026-10-22","kind":"official_docs"},{"id":"s2","url":"https://developers.google.com/workspace/gmail/api/quickstart/js","title":"JavaScript quickstart | Gmail | Google for Developers","accessed":"2026-10-22","kind":"official_docs"},{"id":"s3","url":"https://docs.cloud.google.com/integration-connectors/docs/connectors/gsc_gmail/configure","title":"Gmail | Integration Connectors | Google Cloud Documentation","accessed":"2026-10-22","kind":"official_docs"},{"id":"s4","url":"https://docs.cloud.google.com/contact-center/ccai-platform/docs/oauth-email-google","title":"Configure your email channel for OAuth with Gmail | Google Cloud Contact Center as a Service | Google Cloud Documentation","accessed":"2026-10-22","kind":"official_docs"},{"id":"s5","url":"https://support.google.com/cloud/answer/13464325","title":"Restricted Scopes - Google Cloud Platform Console Help","accessed":"2026-10-22","kind":"official_docs"},{"id":"s6","url":"